# Example entry:
{"id":"pattern-example-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Example: Use mock factories for all test data instead of manual mock objects with 'as Type' assertions.","recommendation":"Create centralized mock factory functions (createMockUser, createMockOrg, etc.) and import them in tests.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"Testing guide","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["testing","mocks","factories"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.test.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-empty-vue-stubs","type":"pattern","fact":"When creating router entries that lazy-load pages not yet implemented, use empty stubs with only <template><div /></template> and no <script> block. Stubs with script code register as 0% coverage.","recommendation":"Create minimal template-only stubs for pages referenced by router but built in later tasks. Replace with full implementation when the task is reached.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #16 coverage gate failure","date":"2026-04-12"}],"tags":["vue","coverage","router","stubs","parallel-tasks"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/pages/**/*.vue"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-subagent-tdd-incomplete","type":"pattern","fact":"Coding subagents frequently complete only the TDD red phase (test files) before hitting context limits, leaving implementation unwritten.","recommendation":"After subagent completion, always verify both test AND implementation files exist. Be prepared to implement from the test spec when the agent only produced tests.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #17 orchestrated execution — WU-004/005 and WU-006/007 agents","date":"2026-04-12"}],"tags":["orchestration","subagents","tdd","context-limits"],"affectedFiles":[],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-bookmark-toggle-on-conflict","type":"pattern","fact":"Bookmark toggle uses INSERT ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING * to detect existence. When the row already exists, RETURNING produces no rows (null). The route interprets null as 'already existed' and deletes it — a clean toggle without a separate existence check query.","recommendation":"Use this ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING * pattern for any idempotent toggle endpoint where you need create-or-remove behavior in a single POST.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #18 Task 3 bookmark routes","date":"2026-04-12"}],"tags":["postgresql","on-conflict","toggle","bookmarks","idempotent"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/db/queries/bookmarks.ts","packages/server/src/routes/bookmarks.ts"],"affectedServices":["createBookmark","bookmarkRoutes"],"createdAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-parallel-route-registration","type":"pattern","fact":"Multiple parallel coding subagents can each add import + app.register() lines to app.ts without merge conflicts. Fastify route registration is additive and order-independent — route plugins don't depend on each other's registration order.","recommendation":"When decomposing server route work into parallel tasks, let each task add its own app.register() call to app.ts. No coordination needed between tasks.","confidence":"medium","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #18 parallel Tasks 2-4 execution","date":"2026-04-12"}],"tags":["fastify","parallel","subagents","app-registration","orchestration"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/app.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-12T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-worktree-setup-forge-monorepo","type":"pattern","fact":"Git worktrees share only .git/ with the main repo; the new worktree's filesystem starts without node_modules or .env. Running npm, vitest, or the server inside a fresh worktree fails until dependencies are installed AND a .env is provided (the server defaults to PORT=3001 and reads DATABASE_URL from .env at the repo root).","recommendation":"After `git worktree add <path> -b feat/<name> main`, run these three commands in the new worktree before doing any test or server work: (1) `npm install` at the worktree root (the monorepo uses npm workspaces so this resolves all three packages), (2) `cp /path/to/main/repo/.env .env`, (3) if the main worktree already has a dev server on :3001, start the feature server on a different port with `PORT=3002 npx tsx packages/server/src/server.ts` and override baseUrl in Bruno via `--env-var baseUrl=http://localhost:3002`.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #3 orchestration setup","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["git","worktree","monorepo","setup","npm","bruno"],"affectedFiles":[".env",".env.example","package.json"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-fastify-plugin-auth-dep-001","type":"pattern","fact":"A Fastify plugin whose hooks or decorators call app.authenticate must declare dependencies: [\"auth-plugin\"] in its fp() config, because authenticate is registered as a preHandler decorator by authPlugin and must exist before downstream plugins reference it.","recommendation":"When a plugin registers decorators that reference app.authenticate (e.g., app.aiGate = [app.authenticate, ...]), wrap it with fastify-plugin and set dependencies: [\"auth-plugin\"] to guarantee load ordering.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"issue #9 LangChain AI autocomplete","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["fastify","plugins","auth","fastify-plugin"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/plugins/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T22:30:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T22:30:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-abort-handlers-helper-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Fastify light-my-request (app.inject) does not let tests emit close on request.raw mid-stream, so the SSE handler's timeout + disconnect abort branches are unreachable via integration tests.","recommendation":"Extract an exported helper like createAbortHandlers(req, slot, timeoutMs) that installs a setTimeout + request.raw.on(\"close\") and returns a cleanup function. Unit-test it with an EventEmitter as the fake request.raw to reach 100% branch coverage.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"issue #9 LangChain AI autocomplete","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["fastify","sse","testing","coverage"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/**/*.ts","packages/server/src/__tests__/routes/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T22:30:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T22:30:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-bruno-assert-syntax","type":"pattern","fact":"Forge's Bruno collection uses declarative 'assert { res.status: eq N }' blocks, matching the existing search/*.bru convention. Chai-style 'tests { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(N) }' is also valid Bruno syntax but is NOT the project standard.","recommendation":"New .bru files MUST use the declarative assert{} form for status checks. The CI lint guard accepts either '^assert \\{' or '^tests \\{' at line start so pre-existing Chai blocks still pass, but new contributions should match the project convention.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #28 WU-004 implementation","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["bruno","testing","syntax","convention"],"affectedFiles":["bruno/**/*.bru"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-bruno-created-vs-fixture-vars","type":"pattern","fact":"When a .bru file creates a new resource (e.g. posts/create-post.bru), its post-response script MUST capture the ID into a created* variable (createdPostId, createdRevisionId), NOT overwrite the fixture variable (postId, revisionId). The fixture variable stays pinned to a seeded UUID so order-independent reads always find a stable target.","recommendation":"Producer .bru: bru.setVar('createdPostId', res.body.post.id). Consumers of the ephemeral post (delete-post, update-post, publish-post) use {{createdPostId}}. Consumers of the fixture (comments, votes, bookmarks, reads) use {{postId}}.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #28 WU-003 variable-lifecycle audit","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["bruno","variables","fixtures","lifecycle","producer-consumer"],"affectedFiles":["bruno/**/*.bru","bruno/environments/*.bru"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-sse-route-shared-helpers-001","type":"pattern","fact":"packages/server/src/routes/ai.ts exports file-scoped SSE helpers (SSE_HEADERS const, TIMEOUT_MS const, writeEvent function, createAbortHandlers factory). A new SSE endpoint (e.g. /generate added alongside /complete) is added by appending a second app.post() handler in the same file that reuses these exports — no new helpers, no refactor, identical abort/timeout semantics across endpoints.","recommendation":"When adding an SSE endpoint to an existing route file with established helpers, EXTEND the file (append a second handler) rather than creating a parallel route file. Reuse SSE_HEADERS + writeEvent + createAbortHandlers + TIMEOUT_MS verbatim. The finally-block cleanup pattern (`cleanupAborts(); slot.release(); reply.raw.end();`) is the contract every SSE handler in the file must follow.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #10 WU-004 route extension","date":"2026-04-14"}],"tags":["fastify","sse","routes","helpers","reuse"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/ai.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-04-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-langchain-runnable-lambda-adapter-001","type":"pattern","fact":"When a LangChain chain input type has OPTIONAL fields (e.g. `language?: string`) but the ChatPromptTemplate references those fields as template variables (e.g. `{language}`), `.format()` requires a string value for every referenced variable — undefined throws 'Missing variable'. Prepending a RunnableLambda in the pipe chain that defaults the optional fields keeps the prompt variable contract stable without forcing callers to provide a default.","recommendation":"Structure the chain as `defaultLambda.pipe(prompt).pipe(model).pipe(parser)` where `defaultLambda = RunnableLambda.from((input) => ({ ...input, language: input.language ?? '' }))`. The lambda is typed explicitly (no `as any`). Verify with two tests (field-omitted vs field-provided) so V8 branch coverage sees both branches of the `??` operator.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #10 WU-003 generate chain","date":"2026-04-14"}],"tags":["langchain","runnable","prompt-template","input-adapter","optional-fields"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/plugins/langchain/chains/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-04-14T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-14T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-ai-acquire-decorator-001","type":"pattern","fact":"When a route needs conditional AI rate limiting (e.g., search is public but AI search needs auth), expose app.aiAcquire(userId): AiSlot | null from the langchain plugin instead of using aiGate as a preHandler. Acquire/release the slot manually in a try/finally block within the route handler.","recommendation":"Use app.aiAcquire() for routes that mix authenticated AI paths with unauthenticated plain paths. Never use aiGate preHandler on mixed routes — it sends 401/429 responses that block the non-AI path.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #11 AI-powered search, WU-004","date":"2026-04-14"}],"tags":["fastify","rate-limiting","ai","langchain"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/plugins/langchain/index.ts","packages/server/src/routes/search.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-04-14T15:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-14T15:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-graceful-ai-fallback-001","type":"pattern","fact":"AI-enhanced endpoints should follow a cascading fallback pattern: try jwtVerify → try aiAcquire → try chain → use filters, with catch → fallback to plain behavior at each step. Users always get results; AI failure is invisible.","recommendation":"Wrap each AI step in its own try/catch or null check. Set a useAi boolean flag to false on any failure and fall through to the non-AI code path. Never surface AI errors to the user on endpoints that have a non-AI fallback.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #11 AI-powered search, WU-004","date":"2026-04-14"}],"tags":["ai","error-handling","fallback","search"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/search.ts"],"affectedServices":["server"],"createdAt":"2026-04-14T15:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-14T15:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-queue-parallel-uploads","type":"pattern","fact":"Concurrent file uploads cause nondeterministic sortOrder when the server assigns order per-request. Unhandled upload rejections also lead to silent failures in drop handlers.","recommendation":"Serialize uploads through a promise queue: chain each uploadFile() call via queue = queue.then(() => uploadFile(...)). Wrap each in try/catch to surface errors. This ensures deterministic ordering and explicit failure handling.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"coderabbit","reference":"PR #37 review","date":"2026-04-27"}],"tags":["file-upload","promise-queue","concurrency","ordering","error-handling"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/components/editor/PostEditor.vue","packages/client/src/stores/files.ts"],"affectedServices":["uploadFile","handleDrop"],"createdAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-db-query-import","type":"pattern","fact":"All DB queries in packages/server/src/db/queries/ import query from '../connection.js' and call query<T>(sql, params). Tests mock '../../db/connection.js' with { query: vi.fn() }. Do NOT use getPool() — it does not exist.","recommendation":"When writing new DB query functions, import { query } from '../connection.js' and call query<T>(). When writing tests, mock '../../db/connection.js' with { query: vi.fn() }.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #6 plan review gate — feasibility reviewer caught getPool() mismatch","date":"2026-04-27"}],"tags":["database","queries","testing","mocking"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/db/queries/**/*.ts","packages/server/src/__tests__/db/queries/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-ssrf-manual-redirect","type":"pattern","fact":"To perform per-hop SSRF checks on redirects, use fetch() with redirect: 'manual'. Intercept 3xx responses, extract Location header, re-resolve DNS for the new hostname, re-check IPs against blocklist, then fetch the next URL. Automatic redirects bypass per-hop IP checks.","recommendation":"For any outbound server-side fetch with SSRF protection, use redirect: 'manual' and implement a redirect loop (max N hops) that re-validates each hop.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #6 link-preview service design and implementation","date":"2026-04-27"}],"tags":["security","ssrf","fetch","redirects"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/services/link-preview.ts"],"affectedServices":["fetchLinkPreview"],"createdAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-cheerio-og-extraction","type":"pattern","fact":"Extract Open Graph metadata from HTML using cheerio: $('meta[property=\"og:title\"]').attr('content') with fallback to $('title').text(). For og:description, fall back to $('meta[name=\"description\"]').attr('content'). Validate og:image is https:// before storing. Estimate reading time: strip HTML via $('body').text(), count words via split(/\\s+/), Math.ceil(words / 200).","recommendation":"Use this pattern for any server-side HTML metadata extraction. Always validate image URLs are https:// to prevent mixed content and tracking pixels.","confidence":"medium","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #6 link-preview parseOpenGraph implementation","date":"2026-04-27"}],"tags":["cheerio","open-graph","html-parsing","metadata"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/services/link-preview.ts"],"affectedServices":["parseOpenGraph"],"createdAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-ipaddr-cidr-matching","type":"pattern","fact":"Use ipaddr.js for SSRF IP blocklist checking: ipaddr.parseCIDR(cidr) returns [addr, bits], then ipaddr.parse(ip).match([network, bits]) checks membership. Must verify addr.kind() === network.kind() before matching to avoid IPv4/IPv6 type mismatch errors.","recommendation":"When checking IPs against CIDR ranges, always compare kind() before match(). Include all RFC-1918 ranges plus 100.64.0.0/10 (CGN), 192.0.0.0/24 (IETF), and IPv6 equivalents (::1/128, fc00::/7, fe80::/10).","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #6 SSRF blocklist implementation, security review feedback","date":"2026-04-27"}],"tags":["security","ssrf","ipaddr","cidr","ip-validation"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/services/link-preview.ts"],"affectedServices":["isIpBlocked"],"createdAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-27T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-optional-jwt-mixed-auth","type":"pattern","fact":"Use try { await request.jwtVerify(); userId = request.user.id } catch {} for Fastify routes that serve both authenticated and unauthenticated users. The identity is resolved opportunistically — auth failures are silently ignored. Then compute isOwner and isPublic flags to gate access per resource type.","recommendation":"Apply this pattern to any endpoint where public resources (e.g., committed files on public posts) and private resources (e.g., staged files) are served from the same route. Check isPublic first to avoid unnecessary 401s on public content.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #38 WU-004 — file endpoint authorization","date":"2026-04-28"}],"tags":["fastify","jwt","authorization","mixed-auth","optional-auth"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/files.ts"],"affectedServices":["fileRoutes"],"createdAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-match-existing-test-mocks","type":"pattern","fact":"When adding tests to an existing test file, always read and match the file's mock infrastructure (vi.hoisted, vi.mock factory patterns, mock variable names). Creating new mock patterns or replacing the file breaks existing coverage. For example, storage.test.ts uses vi.hoisted() for sendMock — new ensureBucket tests must use sendMock, not a fresh mockSend.","recommendation":"Before writing new tests: 1) Read the full existing test file 2) Identify the mock pattern (vi.hoisted vs inline vi.fn, mock variable naming) 3) Use the existing mocks for new assertions. Never create parallel mock infrastructure in the same file.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #38 plan review gate — feasibility reviewer caught storage.test.ts conflict","date":"2026-04-28"}],"tags":["vitest","testing","mocks","vi-hoisted","test-patterns"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/__tests__/**/*.test.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-subagent-interface-validation","type":"pattern","fact":"Coding subagents frequently deviate from a plan's specified TypeScript interfaces (positional args vs options objects, string vs object return types, missing fields). The orchestrator must diff actual exported interfaces against the plan after each subagent completes, not just verify tests pass — tests written by the same subagent will match its own (wrong) interface.","recommendation":"After each coding subagent completes, grep for the key interface/function signatures in the produced code and compare against the plan. Fix mismatches before subsequent work units consume the wrong API.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #8 WU-002/005/006 — manager used code:string instead of files[], composable used positional args, CodeRunner used as-never cast","date":"2026-04-28"}],"tags":["orchestration","subagents","typescript","interfaces","plan-drift"],"affectedFiles":[],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-worker-injectable-factory","type":"pattern","fact":"jsdom lacks the Worker constructor. Client-side services that create Web Workers must accept an injectable WorkerFactory so tests can substitute mock workers implementing postMessage/addEventListener/terminate. Worker entry points that load WASM runtimes use /* v8 ignore start/stop */. Extract all testable logic (API neutralization, message routing, VFS mounting) into separate importable files that can be unit-tested without real WASM.","recommendation":"Structure worker code as: thin entry point (v8-ignored, wires message handlers + loads WASM) + extracted helpers (tested, pure functions). SandboxManager constructor takes WorkerFactory parameter; tests pass vi.fn() mock workers.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #8 WU-002/003 — SandboxManager WorkerFactory pattern, neutralize-apis.ts extraction","date":"2026-04-28"}],"tags":["web-workers","testing","vitest","jsdom","dependency-injection","wasm"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/lib/sandbox/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":["SandboxManager"],"createdAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-component-insertion-selector-stability","type":"pattern","fact":"Adding a new Vue component between existing components can break tests that use CSS class selectors (e.g., wrapper.find('button.text-primary')) if the new component also matches the selector. The test clicks the wrong element silently — assertions fail on unrelated text content, not on the selector itself.","recommendation":"When integrating new components into existing templates, place them AFTER existing interactive elements (not between them) to preserve test selector stability. If you must insert between, verify existing tests still find the right element by checking the test's selector specificity.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"self-reflect","reference":"Issue #8 WU-007 — RunButton with text-primary class broke PostDetail test that used button.text-primary to find inline comment indicator","date":"2026-04-28"}],"tags":["vue","testing","vue-test-utils","selectors","css-classes","component-integration"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/components/**/*.vue","packages/client/src/__tests__/**/*.test.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-per-route-rate-limit-e2e-branch","type":"pattern","fact":"Per-route rate limit decorations in `packages/server/src/routes/auth.ts` (e.g., `{ config: { rateLimit: { max: 3, timeWindow: '1 hour' } } }`) do NOT inherit the global E2E_MODE relaxation that `packages/server/src/plugins/rate-limit.ts:11-15` applies (max 10000/min when E2E_MODE=1). Each strict per-route cap exhausts in a single CI run when the journey + feature suite both fire that endpoint, blocking the 5-consecutive-runs stability gate. The `/login` route already has the relaxation pattern; `/register` was added in issue #46.","recommendation":"When adding any new auth route with a strict per-route rate limit (e.g., max < 10/minute), mirror the E2E_MODE branch pattern from `auth.ts:110-119`: `rateLimit: process.env.E2E_MODE === '1' ? { max: 10_000, timeWindow: <window> } : { max: <strict>, timeWindow: <window> }`. The production branch stays unchanged and remains covered by `packages/server/src/__tests__/plugins/rate-limit.test.ts`.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #46 WU6 register rate-limit stabilization","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["server","rate-limit","e2e","auth","fastify"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/auth.ts","packages/server/src/plugins/rate-limit.ts","packages/server/src/__tests__/plugins/rate-limit.test.ts"],"affectedServices":["auth"],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-cascade-verify-via-post-404","type":"pattern","fact":"After deleting a post via UI, verify cascade by asserting `GET /api/posts/:id` returns 404. Postgres FK-cascade implies all children (comments, votes, bookmarks) are gone with the post.","recommendation":"Don't probe per-resource GETs to verify cascade — they don't exist for votes/bookmarks. The post-404 assertion is sufficient and avoids brittle assumptions about API surface.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU4 delete-cascade","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["e2e","cascade","posts","testing"],"affectedFiles":["e2e/specs/posts/delete-cascade.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-dod-missing-feature-fixme","type":"pattern","fact":"DoD bullets often assume features that don't exist. The canonical pattern is: write the spec asserting the desired behavior, run it to confirm it fails for the right reason, convert to `test.fixme()` with a citation comment, file a follow-up issue with the gap, and reference the issue from the spec.","recommendation":"Don't drop DoD bullets silently. Don't fix server-side gaps if they're out of scope. Use `test.fixme(name, body)` so the spec is preserved as a tombstone and re-enables once the underlying issue lands. Found 6 times in issue #47 (#62 security, #63 tag rendering, #64 link-preview, #65 HomePage panel, #66 presence broadcast, #67 workers=4 contention).","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU2/WU8/WU9/WU10/WU11","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["e2e","dod","fixme","issue-tracking"],"affectedFiles":["e2e/specs/**/*.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-vite-worker-import-suffix","type":"pattern","fact":"Vite's worker plugin only bundles `new Worker(new URL('./w.ts', import.meta.url), opts)` when both arguments are LITERAL — assigning the URL to a variable first defeats the static analyzer and causes Vite to emit the raw `.ts` source as a static asset (or as a TS data: URL), which the browser cannot parse and the worker dies on instantiation. Workers that use dynamic imports also require `worker.format: 'es'` in `vite.config.ts` because the default `iife` format cannot code-split.","recommendation":"Use the `?worker` import suffix as the canonical pattern: `import JsWorker from './js-worker.ts?worker'; return new JsWorker();`. Refactor-safe and avoids the inline-literal trap. Add `worker: { format: 'es' }` to `vite.config.ts` whenever any worker uses `import('...')` (e.g., for `quickjs-emscripten`, `esbuild-wasm`, `pyodide`).","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #70 — useCodeRunner.createWorker split new URL across a variable, Vite emitted js-worker-*.ts raw","date":"2026-04-30"}],"tags":["vite","web-workers","bundling","build","wasm"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/vite.config.ts","packages/client/src/composables/useCodeRunner.ts","packages/client/src/lib/sandbox/workers/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-worker-error-listeners-required","type":"pattern","fact":"A Web Worker that fails to instantiate (build error, syntax error, missing module) emits an `error` event but no `message` event. If the manager only listens for `message`, the failure is silently lost until any execution timeout fires. The same applies to `messageerror` (postMessage deserialization failures).","recommendation":"Every Worker the app constructs must have BOTH `worker.addEventListener('error', ...)` and `worker.addEventListener('messageerror', ...)` registered before postMessage is called. Route both to a single `onError(message)` callback and ensure the same `finished`/`teardown` short-circuit applies as for `done`/`error` messages — otherwise a late worker error after a successful done double-fires onError. Pin both branches with tests.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #70 — SandboxManager only listened for 'message', worker bundling failure was invisible until 30s timeout","date":"2026-04-30"}],"tags":["web-workers","error-handling","observability","sandbox"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/lib/sandbox/manager.ts"],"affectedServices":["SandboxManager"],"createdAt":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"pattern-test-worker-message-contract-on-both-sides","type":"pattern","fact":"When unit tests mock the Worker constructor with `vi.fn()`, they verify what the manager SENDS via postMessage but never run the worker's onmessage handler against the real shape. A divergence between the manager's payload (e.g., `{language, files, entryFile, stdin}`) and the worker's destructure (e.g., `{code, files, ...}`) goes undetected because no test crosses the boundary.","recommendation":"Extract worker-side parsing/lookup into a pure helper module (e.g., `pickEntrySource(files, entryFile)`) and unit-test it directly against the manager's exact payload shape. Define the message contract as a single shared TypeScript type imported by both manager and workers — this surfaces drift at typecheck time. Treat 'manager test calls postMessage with X' as half the contract; the other half is a unit test of 'worker handler accepts X and produces Y'.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #70 — manager sent {entryFile, files} but workers destructured {code}; mocked Worker tests passed for months","date":"2026-04-30"}],"tags":["web-workers","testing","contracts","types","vitest"],"affectedFiles":["packages/client/src/lib/sandbox/**/*.ts","packages/client/src/__tests__/lib/sandbox/**/*.test.ts"],"affectedServices":["SandboxManager"],"createdAt":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
